2.pdf"}]},{"key":"today","kind":"researched","text":"Indonesia's statistics office (BPS) found 284.67 million people in its 2025 intercensal population survey, SUPAS 2025, released in May 2026, after the UN's 2024 figures were made. The UN's mid-2025 figure is 285.72 million, 0.4% higher: the two match.","figure":{"value":284670000,"what":"population of Indonesia from the SUPAS 2025 survey, mid-2025","date":"2025"},"unFigure":{"value":285721236,"what":"UN forecast for 1 July 2025","date":""},"gapPct":0.4,"verdict":"matches","links":[{"label":"BPS-Statistics Indonesia, Berita Resmi Statistik No. 51/05/Th. XXIX: Hasil Survei Penduduk Antar Sensus (SUPAS 2025), 5 May 2026","href":"https://www.bps.go.id/id/pressrelease/2026/05/05/2645/supas-2025--angka-kelahiran-total--tfr--sebesar-2-13---angka-kematian-bayi--imr--sebesar-14-12--dan-persentase-lansia-mencapai-11-97-persen-.html"}],"quotes":[{"text":"Jumlah penduduk Indonesia hasil SUPAS 2025 mencapai 284,67 juta jiwa. Selama periode 2010–2025, jumlah penduduk mengalami peningkatan dari 237,64 juta jiwa hasil SP2010 menjadi 284,67 juta jiwa hasil SUPAS 2025.","href":"https://www.bps.go.id/id/pressrelease/2026/05/05/2645/supas-2025--angka-kelahiran-total--tfr--sebesar-2-13---angka-kematian-bayi--imr--sebesar-14-12--dan-persentase-lansia-mencapai-11-97-persen-.html"}],"accessed":"2026-10-29"},{"key":"net","kind":"researched","text":"The SUPAS 2025 survey found about 537,000 people moved to Indonesia and about one million left over 2022–2025, a net loss of 53 people per 100,000 each year, roughly 150,000 a year. The UN shows a net loss of only about 38,000 a year, so the survey points to more people leaving.","figure":{"value":-151000,"what":"net international migration per year, 2022–2025: survey rate of −53 per 100,000 people a year applied to 284.67 million (our arithmetic)","date":"2022-2025"},"unFigure":{"value":-38469,"what":"UN net migration forecast for 2024 (2022 and 2023 estimates: −37,501 each)","date":""},"gapPct":-74.5,"verdict":"un-higher","links":[{"label":"BPS-Statistics Indonesia, Berita Resmi Statistik No. 51/05/Th. XXIX: Hasil Survei Penduduk Antar Sensus (SUPAS 2025), 5 May 2026","href":"https://www.bps.go.id/id/pressrelease/2026/05/05/2645/supas-2025--angka-kelahiran-total--tfr--sebesar-2-13---angka-kematian-bayi--imr--sebesar-14-12--dan-persentase-lansia-mencapai-11-97-persen-.html"}],"quotes":[{"text":"Hasil SUPAS 2025 menunjukkan bahwa angka migrasi masuk internasional tercatat sebesar 0,61 (rata-rata 61 orang masuk ke Indonesia per 100.000 penduduk tiap tahun) atau mencapai 537 ribu migran internasional yang masuk ke Indonesia pada periode 2022–2025. Pada periode yang sama, angka migrasi keluar internasional adalah sebesar 1,14 (rata-rata 114 orang keluar dari Indonesia per 100.000 penduduk tiap tahun) atau sebanyak satu juta orang migran keluar dari Indonesia.","href":"https://www.bps.go.id/id/pressrelease/2026/05/05/2645/supas-2025--angka-kelahiran-total--tfr--sebesar-2-13---angka-kematian-bayi--imr--sebesar-14-12--dan-persentase-lansia-mencapai-11-97-persen-.html"},{"text":"Angka migrasi neto internasional tercatat sebesar –0,53. Hal tersebut berarti ada pengurangan rata-rata 53 orang setiap 100.000 penduduk Indonesia setiap tahunnya karena migrasi internasional.","href":"https://www.bps.go.id/id/pressrelease/2026/05/05/2645/supas-2025--angka-kelahiran-total--tfr--sebesar-2-13---angka-kematian-bayi--imr--sebesar-14-12--dan-persentase-lansia-mencapai-11-97-persen-.html"}],"accessed":"2026-10-29"}],"links":{"self":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/v1/countries/IDN.json","countries":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/v1/countries.json","risk":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/v1/risk.json","docs":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/","site":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/country/IDN"}}
